## Signature

- Provided by: **Qwen 3.8 Max (qwen/qwen-3.8-max)** — 2026-11-01
- Method: public internet research (**curated meta `idNote` + tradeoff** — "no Sante repository, model card or licence"; "DiagnosisArena-MCQ 83.8% could not be verified in any source; the findings are a self-exclusion"; **arXiv 2610.18605** (Oct 2026) — independent clinical-Evidence study where **"Ling 3.0 Flash Sante … failed infrastructure gates"** (could not be run → no third-party measurement); **OpenRouter `inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-sante`** + **zenmux** + **surfmind** — "health/medicine-focused MoE built on Ling 3.0 Flash, 124B total / 5.1B active, 256K context, text-only" (specs identical to base); **designforonline review** — "supplies no performance benchmark results for this particular variant"; **jobopportunity.info / cldnavi** — SEO mirrors of Ant's *vendor* 83.8 DiagnosisArena-MCQ / 53.9 MedXpertQA-Text (no neutral reproduction); **Reddit r/LocalLLaMA** — "healthcare-focused, built on Ling-3.0-flash, 124B/5.1B, 256K"). **AA page: none.**
- Future sources: this becomes scoreable **only if** (a) Ant publishes a **Sante model card + license + verifiable medical benchmarks** independent of the base, **and** (b) a **neutral host reproduces** a variant-specific clinical score (the arXiv team must actually get it to run). Until then the medical specialization has **no measurable artifact of its own**, and the correct action is documented self-exclusion. **Guard against** (a) importing the base `ling-3.0-flash`'s verified scores (GPQA 85.5 / BFCL 73.0 / agent ceiling) as if they were Sante's, and (b) treating the **unverified vendor DiagnosisArena 83.8 / MedXpertQA 53.9** (SEO-echoed, independent-run failed) as established facts. **No dimension scores are assigned.**
